+# Assumptions — LOO-393
+
+2026-10-06: The exact SSH invocation, Task selector and error from Jack Heart's
+mini attempt are unavailable. Reproduction starts with two isolated Homes and
+must retain this configured acceptance gap.
+
+A receiving machine is assumed to have the repository clone and its definitions.
+Missing Task placement is prepared there; cloning an unrelated repository,
+installation recovery and broad credential provisioning remain outside this Task.
+
+2026-10-07: Jack Heart selected carrying the laptop's chosen account with
+independent renewal, and proposed a detached nohup-like target process holding
+credentials only in memory after the outer process exits. Target-only account
+setup is superseded. Provider-specific renewable grants and simultaneous laptop
+use still need proof; copying rotating refresh credentials is not an established
+solution. If exclusive renewal ownership is necessary, its effect on laptop
+use needs Jack's decision. Credential-owner death requires a fresh handoff;
+the selected design does not persist secrets to survive target reboot.
+
+Jack could not recall the original command/error. Capture a new configured mini
+reproduction rather than asking for the same missing historical detail again.
+
+Legacy bootstrap remains unresolved: absent shared metadata cannot distinguish
+an issue never registered anywhere from an existing Task on an offline Home.
+Preserve old IDs, backfill from their owners, and define admission before
+claiming deterministic IDs alone solve simultaneous first use. This is a
+mechanism gap, not evidence that Jack selected an identity migration.
