@@ -0,0 +1,288 @@
+# Sync Task records through Linear
+
+Draft, reviewed against source on 2026-10-07; mechanism choices below remain
+proposals. Jack Heart requested portable Task records and remote agents that
+survive loss of the originating laptop. The exact mini invocation and error
+remain unavailable; the reported symptom is not a verified incident diagnosis.
+
+## Intended interaction
+
+Illustrative ordinary syntax, not a reproduction of Jack's command:
+
+```sh
+lf ssh mini --task LOO-393 : "Continue the implementation"
+```
+
+Resolve the issue and shared Task identity, reconcile into the mini's SQLite,
+reach or prepare its checkout, hand off scoped credentials into a detached
+target process's memory, verify independent renewal, then launch there.
+Print the target Home, Task, Session and a reconnect command before attaching.
+Closing the connection detaches. Reconnect attaches to that exact Session and
+shows its retained output; it does not repeat the prompt. An explicit Session
+stop remains a separate operation. If it finished while detached, show its
+result and history without starting another turn.
+
+Proposed reconnect surface: `lf ssh mini session attach <session-id>`. This is
+new syntax to implement on the existing Session command. A repeated launch
+with an unresolved startup acknowledgment first reconciles its saved request;
+a deliberately new launch remains a new contribution, subject to existing
+checkout admission. Task identity alone never chooses or replaces a Session.
+
+Remote Git must contain the intended commits. An unpushed branch or edits that
+exist only on the laptop cannot be recovered through Linear. Report the missing
+branch/commit and the push needed; retain the portable Task even when placement
+cannot finish. No implicit commit, push, reset or transfer of uncommitted edits.
+
+## Outcome and owners
+
+Linear issues remain planning authority; Git carries code. SQLite holds each
+Home's Task identity, placement and execution history. A portable record carries
+Task ID, issue ID, workspace slug, agent preference and the PR chain's IDs,
+sequence, slug, branch, base, parent PR link and published GitHub association.
+PR merge/abandonment facts preserve the chain; they are dated evidence, not
+delivery requests. Reobserve GitHub before an action requiring current state.
+It carries no paths, credentials, process claims, workflow cursor, approval,
+publication/merge request, CI verdict or local history. Project ownership is
+resolved from accepted Linear planning on receipt. A pulled GitHub link must
+not fabricate a local publication request merely because the current Rust type
+nests that link inside `PrPublication`.
+
+Existing Tasks and PRs keep their IDs. Receiving a record registers local
+presence without Started, a workflow move, a launch or execution authority.
+SQLite remains the owner of local presence and execution history. Project
+refresh cannot reopen terminal local work; conflicting lifecycle evidence is
+visible and requires the existing explicit transition.
+
+Propose deterministic IDs from immutable Linear issue UUIDs for newly created
+Tasks, and from Task identity plus chain position for new PR entries. This
+avoids random duplicate identities on simultaneous first use; competing PR
+content at one position is still a conflict. Existing opaque IDs take precedence
+when a shared record exists. Backfill those records from their owning Homes.
+Two already-existing identities for one issue must remain unresolved, without
+rewriting local references. Missing attachments alone cannot prove an issue has
+never had a Task on an offline Home. Legacy first-use admission needs an explicit
+bootstrap rule before implementation; do not promise both automatic inference
+and preservation of unknown IDs. Ordinary remote use of an existing Task must
+pull its record, never ask Jack to register it manually.
+
+## Convergence
+
+Use the existing Linear issue attachment integration without overwriting issue
+prose or publishing comments that become direction. Linear documents string
+metadata and an idempotent issue/URL pair: recreating the pair updates the
+attachment. It does not document compare-and-swap. Source:
+[Linear attachments](https://linear.app/developers/attachments), checked October 7.
+
+Propose a versioned canonical record serialized into attachment metadata, with
+a URL containing its content digest. Loopflow writes each revision once and
+checks the digest on read; Linear itself does not make it immutable. Preserve
+all revisions, paginate reads, and report altered or missing ancestry as
+incomplete evidence. Attachment visibility, size limits and growing history
+cost need a provider contract test; the URL must not pretend to host a public
+record that does not exist.
+
+Revisions name parent digests. Ordinary updates have one parent; deliberate
+conflict resolution names every competing tip and records the selected complete
+content. The initial single-parent sketch cannot express that resolution and
+must change. Resolution retains both original candidates; timestamps never
+choose a winner. Concurrent writers can each briefly observe one tip before a
+fork becomes visible: a successful readback proves that revision exists, not
+exclusive global ownership. Sync grants no cross-machine worker exclusion.
+
+Store the accepted baseline content/digest and exact pending revision in the
+same local transaction as portable Task/PR changes. Keep observation time,
+pending state and last failure separate. A digest alone cannot compare offline
+local edits with a changed remote record when the old content is unavailable.
+On response loss, read back the exact digest before retrying identical bytes.
+Never recreate a Task or discard a successful local edit because publication
+failed. Further edits queue behind the retained pending revision.
+
+| Local state against baseline | Incoming state | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Unchanged | Same revision | Update observation health only |
+| Unchanged | Valid descendant | Apply portable fields atomically; retain local facts |
+| Changed | Same revision | Publish retained pending revision |
+| Changed | Descendant or competing tip | Preserve both; expose conflict and resolution |
+| Any | Partial, unavailable or invalid | Keep local facts and original observation age |
+
+Task creation and portable edits attempt publication after their local commit.
+Existing repository planning refresh pulls records for discovered issues and
+retries pending writes; exact Task selection performs targeted reconciliation.
+Catch-up must include retained Tasks outside the current Project and all pages.
+Attachment updates must not depend solely on the issue's `updatedAt` changing.
+Do not add a daemon or use a webhook as the only catch-up mechanism. Status
+reports current, pending, stale/unavailable or conflicted sync separately from
+Task workflow state. Unchanged cached Tasks follow the accepted outage policy;
+missing local identity plus unavailable shared evidence is not an unknown issue.
+
+Opaque Task selectors require resolving their issue from the origin's record
+or the receiving Home's synced inventory. A direct Linear issue selector needs
+neither the origin database nor an origin process once publication succeeds.
+
+## Checkout preparation
+
+Extend the existing Task registration/placement transaction and checkout lease.
+Resolve the clone by repository identity and the selected target repository;
+derive a local path, never copy the origin path. A valid existing placement
+wins. When no local placement exists, reuse an unambiguously matching registered
+branch checkout, including its staged, unstaged and untracked files. Ambiguous
+or occupied placement reports the exact candidate paths without moving bytes.
+
+Fetch and resolve the shared branch before creating a missing checkout. The
+current `restore_task_checkout` permits a base fallback when no local
+`PrStarted` event exists. That inference is invalid on a receiving Home with no
+execution history. Require positive branch/commit evidence there; a missing
+published branch must not silently produce an empty replacement from its base.
+An established local branch is preserved; repeat commands never reset it to a
+new shared tip. Report divergence through existing Git operations.
+
+An incoming chain advance may be accepted as pending shared knowledge while a
+local checkout is busy or dirty. Applying it cannot switch branches or retire
+the current checkout underneath local work. Available target Session/Exec
+evidence controls admission. A matching saved SSH request attaches to its exact
+execution; an independent worker is neither taken over nor duplicated by
+discovery. Unknown local execution remains unknown. Offline evidence from
+another Home cannot establish either liveness or control authority.
+
+## Remote execution
+
+Jack Heart selected a detached target process holding credentials in memory on
+October 7. Implement nohup's lifetime behavior in the existing process launcher:
+start a separate session/process group, survive SIGHUP, disconnect stdin and
+redirect output to the existing target capture. A literal `nohup` wrapper alone
+does not solve credential renewal or inherited pipes. The detached `lf` owns
+the Session driver and an in-memory credential service for its descendants;
+reuse the current broker protocol where appropriate, without a second daemon
+or Work registry. Use the existing Session launch lock and Exec receipts.
+If an interactive terminal needs tmux, it attaches to that same execution and
+receives no secret-bearing shell command or persistent tmux environment.
+Classify agent invocations through the parsed command, covering direct
+prompts, skills, Flow execution and Session continuation; leave foreground
+non-agent commands on their existing transport.
+
+Persist a launch request ID on the origin before SSH, bind it to target Home,
+Task and exact input, and reserve its Session on the target before spawning.
+This request is idempotency metadata on existing execution records, not another
+Work object. Retry the same request under the target launch lock. If a child
+may have started, inspect that exact Session/Exec and preserve uncertainty;
+never allocate another Session because the acknowledgment or PID is missing.
+A startup disconnect before reservation can safely retry; one after reservation
+reuses it. The target must own reservation-to-spawn completion after transport
+loss, including retaining the lock until the child has registered.
+
+Attach only after the target receipt is durable. Capture output on the target,
+independent of the SSH terminal; tmux scrollback is not the history owner.
+Multiple viewers do not gain driver authority. Reconnection uses exact Session
+identity, including from another client with no saved origin receipt. Do not
+silently inject the original prompt again. Explicit interruption follows local
+Session controls; neither an SSH hangup nor a viewer exiting signals the agent.
+The in-memory credential owner survives the outer SSH process exiting. Killing
+that owner or rebooting the target loses its secrets; retain Session/history and
+require a fresh handoff to continue. Do not claim autonomous restart across that
+boundary. Target sleep and installation-state recovery remain LOO-296's scope;
+this Task proves loss of the originating client while the target runs.
+
+## Credentials — selected direction, renewal proof open
+
+Jack Heart chose carrying the selected laptop account to the mini with
+independent renewal, then proposed a nohup-like target process that keeps
+credentials off disk and survives its outer process exiting (2026-10-07).
+This supersedes the recommendation to require a separately configured target
+account. Account selection must preserve the requested identity.
+
+Transfer only the selected provider grant, required GitHub/Linear access and
+explicitly named secrets over SSH into a private pipe/socket consumed by the
+detached owner. Doppler remains the secret source; never send its broad access
+credential. Keep secret bytes out of shell scripts, argv, SQLite, temporary
+files, account homes, tmux configuration, logs and reconnect receipts. Only
+non-secret Session/Exec identity and endpoint location persist. Authenticate
+local IPC by OS ownership/peer identity or an in-memory capability; a reconnect
+client does not need to receive the provider credential. Avoid process dumps
+containing secrets. Application-level no-disk storage does not by itself prove
+that the operating system never swaps memory to disk.
+
+Make the handoff atomic from the launcher's perspective: the target reports
+ready only after all required credential material is received and held by the
+detached owner. Incomplete handoff creates no agent. Lost acknowledgment probes
+the same request and credential owner; it does not launch a second owner or
+replace a live grant. After handoff, the origin broker may exit immediately.
+
+The existing broker lends only access tokens and calls the origin to refresh.
+Moving that broker's process alone therefore cannot meet independent renewal.
+Extend account handling with provider-specific renewal material or an
+independently issued grant for the same account, held only in target memory.
+Resolve its exact scope and expiry before agent launch. Subsequent scoped
+access tokens go to provider children through their existing in-memory channel;
+provider refresh must neither depend on origin connectivity nor write a native
